            <div xml:id="d39">

                <pb facs="0148" n="36" sameAs="frus:frus1935v03/pg36"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.71 Manchuria/82: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in China</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Gauss</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Peiping</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1935-02-01T16:00:00+08:00">February 1, 1935—4
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received February 1—7:51 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>54. Department’s 2, January 4, 6 p.m. Local foreign Commissioner of Posts states
                    that parcel post and money order services between China and “Manchukuo” began
                    today.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Gauss</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
